    ],
    "needsReview": [
      "Default values are marked with ✦ (\"surface ✦\", \"2 ✦\", \"unchecked ✦\", \"default ✦\"). The component set's default is `classic`.",
      "Figma's Radio Group has only 3 axes (size, variant, highContrast: 18 variants) and 6 option-visibility booleans. Selection, the disabled state and the text belong to the Radio (851:29635, 144 variants), which has no contract of its own: its data is in composition.item and in tokens.",
      "The Radio Group description in Figma is correct; the Checkbox Group one is a copy of it and talks about \"radio buttons\".",
      "Tokens read at size 2. Sizes 1 and 3: only radio, indicator, spacing and text style.",
      "The radio is circular, but its corner radius was not read in Figma: there is no radius token in the contract.",
      "highContrast only changes what is selected: classic/surface use accent.12 with a neutral.1 indicator; soft uses accent-alpha with an accent.12 indicator.",
      "opacity on hover/active (0.88, 0.82, 0.92) is fixed in Figma, with no variable. It is the only case where the contract uses opacity; disabled never does.",
      "disabled looks the same for selected and unselected; the text does not change color. classic keeps shadows.shadow-1 also in disabled.",
      "The 160px width and the height are examples. Figma limits to 6 options; in code there is no limit.",
      "Missing: group label, horizontal orientation, error state and required field.",
      "The radio is smaller than 24px: touch area below WCAG 2.5.8."
    ]
  }
